# Every other path falls through to app.html, NOT index.html. index.html is
# `/`'s prerendered markup, stamped data-prerendered="/" - sending every route
# to it would hand `/dashboard` etc. that stamp, which hydrate.ts compares
# against the URL, finds mismatched, and throws away. app.html is the same
# template with an empty <div id="root">, so those routes render like an
# ordinary SPA. Static prerendered files (currently just index.html) still take
# precedence over this catch-all without needing their own line here.
#
# Do not add "!" to force this rule: that would override the static-file
# precedence above, shadowing index.html too and disabling prerendering
# entirely.
/*    /app.html   200
